.TH WEBCOMP "1" "October 2026" "webcomp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
webcomp - Compile files into C source code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webcomp [--strip prefix] fileList >output.c
.SH DESCRIPTION
To enable files to be accessed on embedded systems without a file system, the
\fBwebcomp\fR command converts arbitrary files into C code that
can be compiled and linked into a program. This is useful for applications
that must execute completely from ROM and not access a file system.
This facility can also enhance security by preventing the
modification of files.
.PP
The fileList argument names a file that lists the pathnames of the files to convert, one per line. The C source is written to the standard output.
.PP
When GoAhead is built with ME_ROM enabled, it serves documents from the compiled files instead of the file system. Link the generated source into the program.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\--strip prefix\fR
Specifies a prefix to remove from each of the compiled file names. The \fB--prefix\fR option is an alias for --strip.
.PP
.SH "EXAMPLE"
This example lists the documents directory, its subdirectories and files, and the route and authentication
files, and converts them into C structures in the file romFiles.c. A ROM build reads route.txt and auth.txt
from the compiled files too, so list them. List each path as the server names it: the documents under the
documents directory, here web, and the configuration files relative to the directory the server runs in. Do not
strip the documents directory, since the server looks documents up beneath it.

.PP
    find web route.txt auth.txt -print >fileList
.PP
    webcomp fileList >romFiles.c
.PP
    cc -o romFiles.o romFiles.c

